# source: spec
# spec: docs/protocol/ni-framing.md#payload-classification
# provenance: PV-0005, PV-0202
# kind: ni-payload
# description: A stray NI_PONG\0 received from the server is a keep-alive pong, not a DIAG message, and gets no reply.
# derivation: Rule 3: the payload is exactly the 8 bytes of PV-0005 (exact match per PV-0202); IMPL-NI-9 says the client ignores it and sends nothing.
# expect.class: keepalive-pong
# expect.reply: none
# expect.reply.frame: none
hex:
4E 49 5F 50 4F 4E 47 00                           # N I _ P O N G \0
